{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,215p' ../datomworld/src/cljc/yin/shell/store.cljc | tail -160\nsed -n '636,673p' ../datomworld/src/cljc/yin/shell/dht.cljc\nsed -n '1281,1356p' ../datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing/dht.cljc\npython3 -c 'import re,pathlib,statistics as s; p=pathlib.Path(\\\"build/p2final/durable-wire-final.log\\\").read_text().split()[-1]; f=lambda n: (pathlib.Path(p)/f\\\"dht-{n}.stderr\\\").read_text(); read=lambda n,dir,op: {int(q):int(t) for t,q in re.findall(rf\\\"\"'^:wire ('\"\\\\d+) :{dir} \\\\d+ \\\\{{:op :{op}, :q (\\\\d+)\\\",f(n),re.M)}; a,b,c,d=read(\\\"write\\\",\\\"tx\\\",\\\"ping\\\"),read(\\\"peer\\\",\\\"rx\\\",\\\"ping\\\"),read(\\\"peer\\\",\\\"tx\\\",\\\"reply\\\"),read(\\\"write\\\",\\\"rx\\\",\\\"reply\\\"); print([(len(x),min(x),round(s.median(x)),max(x)) if x else () for x in [[b[q]-a[q] for q in a.keys()&b.keys()],[c[q]-b[q] for q in b.keys()&c.keys()],[d[q]-c[q] for q in c.keys()&d.keys()],[d[q]-a[q] for q in a.keys()&d.keys()]]])'\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yin.shell.store\n  \"The composition's store-selection factory\n   (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md sections 3 and 6).\n\n   The engine's own selection (`yin.repl.store`) knows two stores —\n   `mem` and `file:<dir>` — and answers a generic `dao.jing` content\n   handle for each.  Every storage implementation past those two is a\n   composition's: it owns the scheme, the checked spec, the open, and the\n   transport state the open produces.  This namespace is that factory for\n   the shell compositions, so a host entry point resolves one\n   `--index-store` value against one table instead of asking the engine\n   about a backend the engine must never name.\n\n   It owns no socket, atom, promise, callback, clock or namespace global:\n   selection is a pure dispatch, and the state an open produces is\n   answered as two separate values — the engine's handle and the\n   composition's node — never as one handle with a node inside it.\"\n  (:require [yin.repl.store :as store]\n            [yin.shell.dht :as shell.dht]\n            [yin.shell.query :as shell.query]\n            [yin.shell.session :as session]))\n\n\n(def dht-scheme\n  \"The store scheme the DHT composition registers with the engine's\n   parser, as plain data: a prefix to match, a label for the refusal and\n   help text, and a directory-to-spec projection.  The engine matches the\n   prefix and calls `:parse`; it never learns what the answer means.\"\n  {:prefix shell.dht/dht-scheme\n   :label (str shell.dht/dht-scheme \"<dir>\")\n   :type :dht\n   :parse (fn [dir] {:type :dht :dir dir})})\n\n\n(def schemes\n  \"Every scheme this factory adds to the engine's own two, in the order\n   the parser tries them.\"\n  [dht-scheme])\n\n\n(defn parse-arg\n  \"The `--index-store` value as a spec, over the engine's two schemes and\n   `schemes`: `:mem`, `{:type :file :dir dir}`, or `{:type :dht :dir\n   dir}`.  A missing value, an unknown scheme and an empty directory are\n   refused with every supported form named, so the refusal an operator\n   reads lists the composition's stores too.\"\n  [value]\n  (store/parse-arg value schemes))\n\n\n(defn composition-spec?\n  \"True when `spec` names a store a composition opens rather than one the\n   engine's own selection does.\"\n  [spec]\n  (boolean (and (map? spec)\n                (some #(= (:type %) (:type spec)) schemes))))\n\n\n(defn checked-spec\n  \"Validate an `:index-store-spec` over both selections: the engine's own\n   `:mem` and `{:type :file :dir dir}`, and each registered composition's\n   own checked spec.  Anything else is refused with its reason.\"\n  [spec]\n  (if (composition-spec? spec)\n    (shell.dht/checked-spec spec)\n    (store/checked-spec spec)))\n\n\n(defn open\n  \"Open the store `spec` names, answering the two values of section 3's\n   ownership split:\n\n   ```clojure\n   {:index-store <the generic dao.jing handle the engine is constructed\n                  with>\n    :node <the composition's transport step-owner value, or nil for a\n           store with no transport>\n    :recovery <what the open validated, or nil>\n    :publication-policy <the immutable generic policy of section 5, or nil>\n    :retain-index-on-reset? bool}\n   ```\n\n   `opts` reaches the composition that opens.  They are either its own\n   names (`yin.shell.dht/open`'s `:key`, `:ws`, `:write-heads!`,\n   `:open-store`) or the host driver's neutral ones (`:publisher-key`,\n   `:ws-host`), translated here, so an engine entry point never learns what\n   a composition calls its own inputs.  `:principals`, `:admission` and\n   `:name-env` join the prepared `:link-source` of `:engine-inputs`: the\n   further `yin.repl/create-state` options this composition injects, so a\n   `(reset)` or a `(vm ...)` rebuild reconstructs a session that still\n   resolves signed names and still serves the composition's modules.\n   `:session` is the transport half of the composition session\n   (`yin.shell.session/transport-state`), which a host carries beside its\n   engine value and never inside it.\n\n   A refusal releases whatever the failed open acquired, exactly once, and\n   propagates as itself.\n\n   The engine is handed `:index-store` and never `:node`; the composition\n   keeps the node and steps it\n   (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md sections 3 and 6).\"\n  ([spec] (open spec {}))\n  ([spec opts]\n   (if (composition-spec? spec)\n     (let [_ (when (or (:content-store opts) (:content-client opts))\n               (throw (ex-info \"A composed store cannot use a second content source\"\n                               {:index-store-spec spec})))\n           key (or (:key opts) (:publisher-key opts))\n           opened (shell.dht/open spec {:key key\n                                        :ws (or (:ws opts) (:ws-host opts))\n                                        :write-heads! (:write-heads! opts)\n                                        :open-store (:open-store opts)})]\n       (assoc opened\n              :engine-inputs\n              {:link-source (shell.dht/link-source\n                              spec\n                              {:key key\n                               :principals (:principals opts)\n                               :admission (get opts :admission {})\n                               :name-env (:name-env opts)})\n               :host-modules shell.query/registrations}\n              :session (session/transport-state (:node opened) key)))\n     (let [handle (store/open (store/checked-spec spec))]\n       {:index-store handle\n        :node nil\n        :recovery (:recovery handle)\n        :publication-policy (:publication-policy handle)\n        :retain-index-on-reset? (store/retain-on-reset? handle)\n        :engine-inputs nil\n        :session nil}))))\n\n\n(defn durable?\n  \"True when `store` is a durable directory store the engine's own\n   selection opened (yin.repl.store/durable?).\"\n  [store]\n  (store/durable? store))\n\n\n(defn retain-on-reset?\n  \"True when a session rebuild continues `store`'s published index rather\n   than starting an empty one: the store's declared policy, or the\n   durable directory's own fact when it declares none\n   (yin.repl.store/retain-on-reset?).\"\n  [store]\n  (store/retain-on-reset? store))\n\n\n(defn close!\n  \"Release `store`'s lifecycle resources.  Idempotent, and the one place a\n   composition's resource owner closes the store it opened\n   (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md sections 3 and 6).\"\n  [store]\n  (store/close! store))\n  ([spec {:keys [key ws write-heads! open-store]}]\n   (let [{:keys [dir peers publish? bind-host bind-port max-inbound-bytes\n                 manifest bind!]\n          :as checked} (checked-spec spec)\n         follow (checked-follow checked)\n         base ((or open-store durable/open) dir)\n         [node records]\n         (try\n           (when-some [why (refused-head dir manifest\n                                         (get-in base [:recovery :manifest]))]\n             (throw (ex-info why {:dir dir :manifest manifest})))\n           (let [records (heads-records dir follow)]\n             [(dht/join {:local base\n                         :peers peers\n                         :publish? publish?\n                         :bind-host bind-host\n                         :bind-port bind-port\n                         :max-inbound-bytes max-inbound-bytes\n                         :repair-slots default-repair-slots\n                         :bind! (or bind! (dht/default-bind))})\n              records])\n           (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n             (quietly! #(durable/close! base))\n             (throw e)))]\n     ;; from here the node owns the store and holds a socket\n     (try\n       (when (seq peers)\n         ;; Peek at the immediate lifecycle result. The tick owner still\n         ;; reads successful binds and asynchronous results with this cursor.\n         (let [traffic (get-in node [:composition :traffic])\n               event (:dao.stream/value (stream/next traffic (:traffic-cursor node)))]\n           (when (= :dao.stream.datagram/bind-failed (:dao.stream.datagram/event event))\n             (let [reason (str (:dao.stream.datagram/reason event))]\n               (throw (ex-info (str \"dht: refused: the socket could not bind: \" reason)\n                               {:dir dir :reason reason}))))))\n       (let [[index-store node]\n             (compose node base checked follow records\n                      {:key key :ws ws :write-heads! write-heads!})]\n\n(defn state\n  \"Validate a composition (section 2) and return the DHT's state: a plain\n   map of its handles, cursors, limits, routing table and pending tables.\n   Throws on a composition defect; performs no stream operation.\"\n  [composition]\n  (let [c (merge defaults composition)\n        {:keys [local requests answers facts ticks traffic datagrams]} c\n        ack-peers (::ack-peers c)]\n    (when-not (and (ifn? (:put-bytes-fn local)) (ifn? (:get-bytes-fn local)))\n      (throw (defect \"composition needs a :local byte-store handle\"\n               {:local local})))\n    (when-not (and requests (stream/reader? requests))\n      (throw (defect \"composition needs a :requests reader\" {})))\n    (when-not (and answers (stream/writer? answers))\n      (throw (defect \"composition needs an :answers writer\" {})))\n    (when-not (and facts (stream/writer? facts))\n      (throw (defect \"composition needs a :facts writer\" {})))\n    (when-not (and ticks (stream/reader? ticks))\n      (throw (defect \"composition needs a :ticks reader\" {})))\n    (when-not (= (some? traffic) (some? datagrams))\n      (throw (defect \":traffic and :datagrams are composed together or not\"\n               {})))\n    (when (and traffic\n               (not (and (stream/reader? traffic) (stream/writer? datagrams))))\n      (throw (defect \":traffic must be a reader and :datagrams a writer\" {})))\n    (when (and traffic\n               (not (and (wire/byte-payload? (::secret c))\n                         (<= 32 (byte-count (::secret c))))))\n      (throw (defect \"socket composition needs a secret of at least 32 bytes\" {})))\n    (when (and traffic\n               (not (and (integer? (::max-inbound-bytes c))\n                         (<= 0 (::max-inbound-bytes c)))))\n      (throw (defect \"socket composition needs a nonnegative max-inbound-bytes\" {})))\n    (when-not (node-id? (::id c))\n      (throw (defect \"the node id must be 64 lowercase hex characters\"\n               {:id (::id c)})))\n    (when-not (datagram/ip-literal? (::bind-host c))\n      (throw (defect \"bind-host must be an IP literal\"\n               {:bind-host (::bind-host c)})))\n    (when-not (and (integer? ack-peers) (<= 2 ack-peers kad/k))\n      (throw (defect \"ack-peers must be an integer from 2 to k\"\n               {:ack-peers ack-peers, :k kad/k})))\n    (merge c\n           {:requests-cursor (get c :requests-cursor :dao.stream/oldest)\n            :ticks-cursor (get c :ticks-cursor :dao.stream/oldest)\n            :traffic-cursor (get c :traffic-cursor :dao.stream/oldest)\n            :now nil\n            :table {}\n            :cookies {}\n            :seen {}\n            :queries {}\n            :query-index {}\n            :partial {}\n            :partial-order []\n            :inbound-bytes 0\n            :inbound-addresses #{}\n            :writes {}\n            :gets {}\n            :advance-cursor nil\n            :out-answers []\n            :out-facts []})))\n\n\n(defn step\n  \"The only thing that advances the DHT, in section 2's order, each stage\n   bounded by budget: drain ticks; read traffic; read requests; advance\n   pending work; append answers and facts. Returns the successor state.\n   This is an interpreter step -- it performs stream operations -- under\n   a single-owner precondition: one caller, one state thread.\"\n  [state budget]\n  (-> state\n      (drain :ticks :ticks-cursor :ticks budget on-tick)\n      (cond-> (:traffic state)\n        (drain :traffic :traffic-cursor :traffic budget on-traffic))\n      (drain :requests :requests-cursor :requests budget on-request-value)\npython3: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\npython3: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-uovvXo24' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-27 01:44:40.403 xcodebuild[51338:2966115]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-27 01:44:40.729 xcodebuild[51338:2966109] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\npython3: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\npython3: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-Nn4V5VK8' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-27 01:44:41.662 xcodebuild[51348:2966233]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-27 01:44:41.874 xcodebuild[51348:2966219] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\n[(44, 10548, 12494, 14423), (44, 1947, 4780, 8091), (20, 13, 138, 268), (20, 15218, 15978, 16986)]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"agent_message","text":"The wire trace shows the ping and cookie reply reached their destinations, but matching replies took 15–17 seconds during live owner turns. The existing query window is 500 ms and the publication window is five seconds. I’ll test longer Gambit-specific windows while keeping the protocol and quorum unchanged."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"set -eu\ncp test/gambit/fixtures/yin-durable.jolt build/p2final/durable-timing-check.jolt\ncat >>build/p2final/durable-timing-check.jolt <<'EOF'\n\n(def \"'^:private timed-dht-limits\n  {:dao.jing.dht/query-ticks 30000\n   :dao.jing.dht/ack-ticks 90000\n   :dao.jing.dht/get-ticks 90000})\n(defn- timed-durable-open [spec opts]\n  (let [opened (durable-test-open spec opts)\n        node (:node opened)]\n    (if (:seam node)\n      (let [node (update node :composition merge timed-dht-limits)]\n        (-> opened\n            (assoc :node node)\n            (assoc-in [:session :node] node)))\n      opened)))\n(defn -main [& args]\n  (main/main! args (assoc composition :open timed-durable-open)))\nEOF\nsed '\"'s@../../test/gambit/fixtures/yin-durable\\\\.jolt@durable-timing-check.jolt@' build/p2final/durable-compiled-check.ss >build/p2final/durable-timing-check.ss\nprefix=\\\"\"'$HOME/.local/share/mise/installs/gambit/4.9.8\"\nJOLT_GAMBIT_YIN_MODE=compiled GAMBIT_DHT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=3600 caffeinate -i sh host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh 4800 python3 build/p2final/run-durable-diagnostic.py \"$prefix/bin/gsi\" build/p2final/durable-timing-check.ss >build/p2final/durable-timing-check.log 2>build/p2final/durable-timing-check.stderr'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
